## 3️⃣ DIY: Call the Geocoding API yourself and build a custom UI

If you need **full control over the UI** (e.g., a modal, a sidebar, a voice-activated search, or you want to combine results from multiple providers), you can skip the bundled control and talk directly to the **Mapbox Geocoding API** (or any other geocoder) yourself.

### 3.1 Mapbox Geocoding API basics

```
GET https://api.mapbox.com/geocoding/v5/mapbox.places/<query>.json
  ?access_token=YOUR_TOKEN
  &autocomplete=true
  &proximity=lon,lat
  &bbox=minLon,minLat,maxLon,maxLat
  &types=place,address,postcode
  &language=en
  &limit=5
```

**Response** is a GeoJSON FeatureCollection. Each feature has:

* `place_name` – human-readable address
* `center` – `[lon, lat]`
* `bbox` – optional bounding box
* `properties` – e.g., `category`, `address`, `text`

### 3.2 Minimal vanilla-JS UI

```html
<input id="search" type="text" placeholder="Search…" style="position:absolute;top:10px;left:10px;z-index:1;padding:6px;width:250px;">
<div id="results" style="position:absolute;top:40px;left:10px;z-index:1;background:#fff;max-height:200px;overflow:auto;"></div>

<script>
const token = 'YOUR_MAPBOX_ACCESS_TOKEN';
const input = document.getElementById('search');
const resultsDiv = document.getElementById('results');

let abortCtrl = null;

input.addEventListener('input', debounce(async e => {
  const query = e.target.value.trim();
  if (!query) { resultsDiv.innerHTML = ''; return; }

  // Cancel previous request
  if (abortCtrl) abortCtrl.abort();
  abortCtrl = new AbortController();

  const url = new URL(`https://api.mapbox.com/geocoding/v5/mapbox.places/${encodeURIComponent(query)}.json`);
  url.search = new URLSearchParams({
    access_token: token,
    autocomplete: true,
    limit: 6,
    // proximity: '-122.447303,37.753574', // optional bias
    // language: 'en',
    // types: 'address,place,postcode'
  });

  try {
    const resp = await fetch(url, { signal: abortCtrl.signal });
    const data = await resp.json();
    renderResults(data.features);
  } catch (err) {
    if (err.name !== 'AbortError') console.error(err);
  }
}, 250));

function renderResults(features) {
  resultsDiv.innerHTML = '';
  if (!features.length) {
    resultsDiv.textContent = 'No results';
    return;
  }
  const ul = document.createElement('ul');
  ul.style.listStyle = 'none';
  ul.style.margin = 0;
  ul.style.padding = 0;
  features.forEach(f => {
    const li = document.createElement('li');
    li.textContent = f.place_name;
    li.style.padding = '4px 8px';
    li.style.cursor = 'pointer';
    li.addEventListener('click', () => {
      // Fly to the result and add a marker
      map.flyTo({ center: f.center, zoom: 14 });
      new mapboxgl.Marker().setLngLat(f.center).addTo(map);
      resultsDiv.innerHTML = '';
      input.value = f.place_name;
    });
    ul.appendChild(li);
  });
  resultsDiv.appendChild(ul);
}

// Simple debounce helper
function debounce(fn, ms) {
  let timeout;
  return (...args) => {
    clearTimeout(timeout);
    timeout = setTimeout(() => fn.apply(this, args), ms);
  };
}
</script>
```

**Why go DIY?**

* **Custom layout** – you can embed the search inside a sidebar, a modal, or a floating button.
* **Multiple providers** – call Mapbox *and* a secondary service (e.g., OpenStreetMap Nominatim, Pelias, Algolia Places) and merge results.
* **Non-Mapbox data** – you might want to search your own POI database first, then fall back to Mapbox.
* **Advanced UX** – voice input, keyboard shortcuts, “search as you type” with debouncing, custom result cards with images, etc.

